* Step 5: After resuming, the schedule G value is reset to the initial default of 3000. I believe this is intentional, because the resumption might be taking place under changed circumstances and may be happening after considerable time has elapsed after the original run. But I wonder what happens if the interruption coincidentally happens to occur just before the normal end of an interval... then there might not be enough time left to do an accurate benchmark to recalibrate sched G for the next interval. Or perhaps I am misunderstandinghow it works.
